[[File:Fighting the King Black Dragon.png|thumb|400px|A group of players take on the King Black Dragon.]]
'''{{Colour|red|Warning}}:''' While the King Black Dragon's lair is not considered to be a part of the Wilderness, you will need to cross a short distance in deep level 42-Wilderness that is commonly patrolled by [[Player killers]]. Do not bring any items into the Wilderness you are not willing to lose.

The [[King Black Dragon]], commonly referred to as KBD, is a three-headed dragon located in [[King Black Dragon Lair|his lair]] deep in the [[Wilderness]]. The King Black Dragon has a [[combat level]] of 276, which makes him one of the strongest [[Dragon (race)|dragons]] in ''[[Old School RuneScape]]''. Players should always take an [[anti-dragon shield]] as his [[dragonfire]] breath is very deadly without protection. The King Black Dragon can also be killed as an alternative for a [[black dragon]] [[Slayer task]], '''except''' those given by [[Krystilia]].

==Requirements==
There are no strict requirements to killing the King Black Dragon.

===Recommendations===
*High [[combat]] stats. Although not required, the skill levels below are advised:
**If using [[Melee]]:
***Level {{SCP|Attack|80}} or higher
***Level {{SCP|Strength|80}} or higher
***Level {{SCP|Hitpoints|70}} or higher
***Level {{SCP|Prayer|70}} or higher for the [[Piety]] prayer
**If using [[Ranged]]:
***Level {{SCP|Ranged|80}} or higher
***Level {{SCP|Hitpoints|70}} or higher
***Level {{SCP|Prayer|74}} or higher for the [[Rigour]] prayer
*Partial completion of {{SCP|Quest}} [[Dragon Slayer I]] for access to [[anti-dragon shield]]s.
*Completion of {{SCP|Quest}} [[Slug Menace]] for access to [[proselyte armour]].

==Transportation==
[[File:KBD Routes.png|thumb|400px|The routes that lead to the King Black Dragon Lair. The burning amulet route is blue. The obelisk route is yellow. The Ghorrock Teleport route is orange. The waka canoe route is green.]]
The [[King Black Dragon]] resides in the [[King Black Dragon Lair]], which is '''not''' in the [[Wilderness]], so [[teleport]]s can be used inside if needed. However, its lair can only be accessed by travelling through the Wilderness, so take precautions and don't bring any items you're not willing to lose. In the event that you are teleblocked, you '''cannot''' use the [[Lever (King Black Dragon Lair)|lever]] to escape.

Using any of the following methods, ordered from quickest to slowest, will lead players to the King Black Dragon Lair:
*[[Burning amulet]]
*#Use a burning amulet to teleport to the [[Lava Maze]].
*#Run west and then north along the fence.
*#Go through the gate and climb down the ladder.
*[[Player-owned house]] [[Obelisk (Construction)|obelisk]] - Requires completion of the {{SCP|Diary}} [[Wilderness Diary|hard Wilderness Diary]] or better for effective use
*#Select level 44 as the teleport destination of the obelisk in the [[superior garden]].
*#Right-click the Wilderness Obelisk and select teleport to destination.
*#Run south-east, go through the gate and climb down the ladder.
*[[Ghorrock Teleport]] ([[Ghorrock teleport (tablet)|tablet]]) ([[Portal chamber|portal]]) - Requires completion of the {{SCP|Quest}} [[Desert Treasure I]] quest.
*#Use the Ghorrock Teleport (or tablet or portal) to teleport to the [[Frozen Waste Plateau]], near the (level 44) [[Wilderness Obelisk]] west of the KBD lair.
*#Run south-east, go through the gate and climb down the ladder.
*[[Games necklace]] and [[Wilderness Obelisk]] - Requires completion of the {{SCP|Diary}} [[Wilderness Diary|hard Wilderness Diary]] or better for effective use
*#Use a games necklace to teleport to the [[Corporeal Beast]]'s lair.
*#Leave the cave and run south-east to the Wilderness Obelisk.
*#Select level 44 as the teleport destination of the Wilderness Obelisk.
*#Right-click the Wilderness Obelisk and select teleport to destination.
*#Run south-east, go through the gate and climb down the ladder.
*[[Waka canoe]] - This requires a woodcutting [[axe]] as well as level {{SCP|Woodcutting|57}} or better.
*#Use the canoe station in [[Edgeville]] to travel to the [[Wilderness pond]] in level 35 Wilderness.
*#Run west-north-west to and then north along the fence.
*#Go through the gate and climb down the ladder.

Down the stairs, there is a lever players can pull to enter the King Black Dragon Lair.

==Mechanics==
===Attack styles===
[[File:KBD Melee and Dragonfire.gif|thumb|right|The King Black Dragon's Melee and fiery breath attacks.|200px]]
[[File:KBD Special Breaths.gif|thumb|right|The King Black Dragon using his fiery, toxic and shocking breath attacks.|200px]]
The King Black Dragon attacks with [[Melee]] and [[dragonfire]] attacks. King Black Dragon will use a melee attack 1/3 of the time provided the target is in melee range. Otherwise, a dragonfire attack is used with a 50% chance of a special dragonfire attack. <ref>{{PlainCiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1698712575108579369|date=4 September 2023|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/100462|archivedate=4 September 2023|quote=Yes, if it's in melee range, it's got a 1/3 chance of doing melee, 1/3 chance of doing fire and 1/3 of doing one of the ice/toxic/shocking attacks.}}</ref>All three special dragonfires (Toxic, Shocking, and Icy breath) are equally common, each with a 1/9 incidence in melee range or a 1/6 incidence outside of melee range.<ref>{{PlainCiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1698712744508154162|date=4 September 2023|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/103193|archivedate=4 September 2023|quote=If it gets to one of the ice/toxic/shocking attacks, normally they have equal chances.}}</ref> 
*The Melee attack is only used when the player is standing in Melee distance and can hit up to 25.
**The [[Protect from Melee]] prayer will negate all damage from this attack.
*The fiery breath attack can deal up to 65 damage. [[Dragonfire#Protection|Antifire shields]], [[Dragonfire#Protection|antifire potions]], and [[Protect from Magic]], or a combination of these, will partially negate the damage from this attack.
*There are three different special dragonfire attacks. Each of these attacks can deal up to 50 damage and have a 50% chance upon a successful hit to inflict a unique effect<ref>{{PlainCiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1698965398287212751|date=5 September 2023|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/98756|archivedate=5 September 2023|quote=Protection that reduces the damage, such as shields or the prayer. Without any of that, the chance would be higher - up to 1/2.}}</ref>. Antifire shields and Protect from Magic, or a combination of these, will partly negate the damage from this attack and reduce the effect chance to 1 in 8.<ref>{{PlainCiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1698729370817347816|date=5 September 2023|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/107077|archivedate=5 September 2023|quote=That one depends on your protection. It'll usually be 1/8 for a well-protected player.}}</ref>
**Toxic breath inflicts poison to the player, starting at 8 damage.
**Shocking breath drains two levels off of all the player's stats.
**Icy breath freezes the player for 10 ticks (6 seconds).

